                    "text": "in 2 (signal/float) Ramp Time in SAMPLES"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "code": "\r\nexpApprox(x)\n{\n\tx = 1 + (0.062500309 + (0.0019527233 + (0.0000408663 + (0.00000060184965 + 0.000000010856791*x)*x)*x)*x)*x;\n\tx *= x; x *= x; x *= x;\n\treturn x*x;\n}\r\n\r\n// like MSP [curve~], exact destination\n// Miller Puckette, David Zicarelli, Graham Wakefield, me\n// the only side effect of using 'expA()' approximation (with no compensation offsets)...\n// ...is that 'curvature' values < -0.95 && > 0.95 produce curves not quite as steep as the original...\n// ...this is totally fine by me, and probably worth it\n// N.B. - this is expensive in gen~ and you should probably avoid using it\neviCurve(target, duration, curvature)\t\t// target, duration in samples, curvature -1..1\n{\r\n    History init(1);\n\tHistory v(0), v0(0), v1(0), vrange(0);\t\t\t// value: current, from, to, range\n\tHistory samplecount(0), samplesremain(0);\t\t// samples elapsed, samples remaining\n\tHistory divFactorDuration(0), divExpCurve(0);\t// cached values to speed up per-sample loop\n\t// magic numbers\n\tRFACTOR\t\t= 4.3478260869565215;\t\t// float(1 / 0.23)\n\tPFACTOR\t\t= 5;\n\tDIV_RFACTOR\t= 0.013104405582925738;\t\t// float(1 / (exp(RFACTOR) - 1))\n\tSFACTOR\t\t= 0.005;\n\n\t// calculated only when a new target is set\n\tif (change(target)) {\n\t\t// starting a new ramp\n\t\tsamplecount = 0;\n\t\t// duration in samples\n\t\tsamplesremain = duration * (1 - init);\n\t\t// ramp start & end values\n\t\tv0, v1 = v, target;\n\t\t// ramp range\n\t\tvrange = v1 - v0;\n\t\t// nonlinear mapping of -1 to 1 curve factor\n\t\tf = 1 - abs(curvature);\n\t\tf = PFACTOR * (expApprox(f * RFACTOR) - 1) * DIV_RFACTOR;\n\t\ts = sign(curvature);\n\t\tp = (s != 0) ? (s * f) : f;\t\t\t// must do this to avoid 'curvature == 0' issue\n\t\t// bypass really sharp curves\n\t\t// 'p = fixdenorm(p);' does not work ? or is it the expApprox() ?\n\t\tp = (p >= 0 && p < SFACTOR) ? SFACTOR : ((p < 0 && p > -SFACTOR) ? -SFACTOR : p);\n\t\t// cached factors for the per-sample curve calculation\n\t\tdivExpCurve = 1 / (expApprox(1 / p) - 1);\n\t\tdivFactorDuration = 1 / (samplesremain * p);\n\t}\n\n\tvalue, notify = 0;\n\t// per sample calculation\n\tif (samplesremain > 0.5) {\t\t\t\t// still ramping\n\t\tvalue\t= v;\n\t\tnotify\t= init;\t\n\t\t// compute next ramp sample\n\t\tsamplecount += 1;\n\t\tsamplesremain -= 1;\n\t\t// compute curvature\n\t\tcurv = (expApprox(samplecount * divFactorDuration) - 1) * divExpCurve;\n\t\t// scale to the output range & integrate\n\t\tv += (v0 - v) + (curv * vrange);\n\t} else {\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// no longer ramping\n\t\tv\t\t= v1;// + (target * init);\n\t\tvalue\t= v;\n\t\tnotify\t= 1 - init;\n\t}\n\r\n    init = 0;\n\treturn value, notify;\n}\r\n\r\nout1, out2 = eviCurve(in1, in2, in3);\r\n\r\n",
                    "fontface": 0,
                    "fontname": "<Monospaced>",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-3",
